  "hindi": "दधिक्रावन् का ही हम अब कीर्तन करेंगे; सब उषाएँ ही मुझे ठीक करें; जलों के, अग्नि के, उषा के, सूर्य के, बृहस्पति के, आङ्गिरस के, विजयी के।",
  "english": "Of Dadhikrāvan indeed we shall now speak in praise; may all the Dawns indeed set me right; of the waters, of Agni, of the Dawn, of the Sun, of Bṛhaspati, of the Āṅgirasa, of the victorious one.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Obscure. The genitive dadhikrāvṇaḥ with carkirāma is read as 'celebrate (of) Dadhikrāvan'. The genitive list in line 2 (apām, agneḥ, uṣasaḥ, sūryasya, bṛhaspateḥ, āṅgirasasya, jiṣṇoḥ) has no governing word in the verse; it is translated as printed without supplying one. Whether āṅgirasasya and jiṣṇoḥ belong to Bṛhaspati or to Dadhikrāvan is unclear.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
